# REGRESSION (was todo/t0840, found while widening its net): `Channel[T]` is a
# refcount handle whose `clone_fn` is the by-VALUE incref
# (`TypeMetadata::set_refcount_clone_fn`, the single writer for that axis) —
# but the generic `.clone()` lowering handed it `&handle`, so
# `gorget_channel_retain` increfed the CALLER'S STACK SLOT. Everything after
# that read `ch->buf` as a channel: `send` hung, or tripped
# `__pthread_mutex_lock_full: Assertion 'e != ESRCH || !robust'`.
#
# `Shared`/`Weak` escaped only because their own dispatch arms pass the handle
# by value by hand; `Channel` has no such arm and got the generic path, which
# is exactly why the fix belongs in the generic path (read
# `is_refcount_clone_type`) and not in a fourth hand-written arm.
#
# ⚠ The first half needs NO container at all — that is the point: the defect
# was in `.clone()`, and the container merely made it visible.
#
# CELL: handle=Channel · payload=int · {bare clone, Vector element}.

void main():
    # bare clone — no container involved
    Channel[int] c = Channel[int](4)
    Channel[int] c2 = c.clone()
    c2.send(7)
    print(f"{c.recv()}")

    # the same handle inside a Vector, sent through the element view
    Channel[int] d = Channel[int](4)
    Vector[Channel[int]] all = []
    all.push(d.clone())
    print(f"{all.len()}")
    all.get(0).unwrap().send(9)
    print(f"{d.recv()}")
